#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:0
msgid ""
"Understand refresh awareness, which manages automatic snap updates for "
"running desktop applications with in-place or deferred updates and "
"notifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:8
msgid "Refresh awareness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:10
msgid ""
"Snaps update automatically, and by default, the *snapd* daemon checks for "
"updates 4 times a day. Each update check is called a *refresh* and is "
"described in more detail in {ref}`Managing updates <how-to-guides-work-with-"
"snaps-manage-updates>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:12
msgid ""
"If a refresh occurs while an affected desktop application is running, "
"**refresh app awareness** helps to mitigate any potential issues, using a "
"combination of in-place updates, deferred updates, and desktop notifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:14
msgid "Refresh awareness requires snapd _2.57+_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:17
msgid ""
"{ref}`Service management <how-to-guides-manage-snaps-control-services>` is "
"not affected, as services are started and stopped manually as part of the "
"refresh process, unless a specific _endure_ value has been embedded into the "
"snap by the snap developer. See [snapcraft.yaml refresh-mode](https://"
"documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/reference/snapcraft-yaml/#apps."
"%3Capp-name%3E.refresh-mode) for further details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:20
msgid "In-place updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:22
msgid ""
"If an application is running when an automatic refresh detects an update, "
"the new snap revision is downloaded in the background to minimise the "
"refresh time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:24
msgid ""
"When the download is complete, the user is notified of the pending update "
"and a snap refresh is triggered when the application stops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:26
msgid ""
"![Snap pending update notification](https://assets.ubuntu.com/v1/6bcfcc2b-"
"firefox-pending.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:26
msgid "Snap pending update notification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:28
msgid ""
"Once the snap has been refreshed, an additional notification informs the "
"user that the new snap revision is ready to be used (requires snapd "
"*2.59.2+*)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:30
msgid ""
"In-place updates only work with automatic refreshes, and not when a refresh "
"is triggered manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:32
msgid "Deferred updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:34
msgid ""
"An update can be postponed for up to 14 days for a running application. The "
"update will be either applied when the application closes, during next "
"automatic refresh occurs without the application running, or after 14 days "
"even if the application remains active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:36
msgid ""
"After closing the affected application, the refresh can be triggered "
"manually with the `snap refresh` command, either globally for all snaps, or "
"with the specific snap name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:38
msgid "snap refresh <snap-name>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:42
msgid ""
"If a manual refresh detects the application is still running, the error "
"output will include the detected process ids of the running applications:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:44
msgid ""
"error: cannot refresh \"firefox\": snap \"firefox\" has running apps "
"(firefox), pids:\n"
"       1639,1854,1912,1932,3514,3632,5814,5870\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:49
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Managing updates <how-to-guides-work-with-snaps-manage-updates>` "
"for more details controlling update frequencies, and holding updates for any "
"period of time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:51
msgid "Desktop notifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:53
msgid ""
"While an affected application is running, each refresh attempt will trigger "
"a desktop notification to inform the user that the app should be closed to "
"avoid disruption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:55
msgid ""
"On the default Ubuntu GNOME desktop, notifications can be modified and "
"disabled by selecting Notifications from the Settings application and "
"selecting the _Snapd User Session Agent_ application:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:57
msgid ""
"![Snapd User Session Agent Gnome Notification Settings](https://"
"assets.ubuntu.com/v1/a417893f-snapd-notifications.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:57
msgid "Snapd User Session Agent Gnome Notification Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:59
msgid "Other desktop environments have equivalent functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/refresh-awareness.md:61
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Refresh awareness security policy <ref-security-policies_refresh-"
"awareness>` for details on how refresh updates accommodate confinement and "
"security policy requirements."
msgstr ""
